# Multimodal Analysis

The multimodal framework integrated:

* Foundation model embeddings (UNI)
* Nuclear morphometric features
* Clinicopathological variables

This strategy substantially improved classification performance and generalization.

## Internal Test Performance

* **Overall Accuracy:** 0.91
* **Weighted Precision:** 0.91
* **Weighted Recall:** 0.91
* **Weighted F1-score:** 0.91
* **Balanced Accuracy:** 0.90
* **Cohen’s Kappa:** 0.88
* **Sensitivity:** 0.91
* **Specificity:** 0.94

## ROC-AUC Performance

| Diagnostic Category            | AUC   |
| ------------------------------ | ----- |
| Aggressive B-cell lymphoma     | 0.905 |
| NK/T-cell lymphoma             | 0.880 |
| Indolent/small B-cell lymphoma | 0.870 |
| Reactive lesions               | 0.811 |

The multimodal model demonstrated markedly reduced inter-class confusion and improved latent feature separation compared with the unimodal model.

